WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.073
- [Kelly] I like it.

00:00:01.073 --> 00:00:03.570
Have y'all, have y'all ever met before?

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.707
- [Sam] What's that? No, never.

00:00:04.707 --> 00:00:05.792
- No, no.
- Lovely to meet you.

00:00:05.792 --> 00:00:08.152
- [Kelly] Well, you did a really
great job of coordinating.

00:00:08.152 --> 00:00:08.985
- Yeah.
- You are?

00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:09.818
- Yeah.

00:00:09.818 --> 00:00:10.661
- Did he just say, "Are you English?"

00:00:10.661 --> 00:00:11.759
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:12.592
I love that.

00:00:12.592 --> 00:00:13.425
- Actually, no, I don't
wanna embarrass you,

00:00:13.425 --> 00:00:17.250
but we did follow each other
on Twitter a few years ago.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.083
- [Kelly] Oh, y'all did?

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:19.410
- Oh, my gosh.
- Um...

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.981
- He broke up with you.
- What happened?

00:00:20.981 --> 00:00:21.814
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:00:21.814 --> 00:00:22.647
No, what happened?

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:23.480
- I don't think you do anymore.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.313
- No.

00:00:24.313 --> 00:00:25.146
- No, do you know what?

00:00:25.146 --> 00:00:26.552
We never, we never
actually spoke on Twitter.

00:00:26.552 --> 00:00:27.941
- Oh, I think...
- Sorry, this is...

00:00:27.941 --> 00:00:28.890
(audience laughs)
- No, I don't go on Twitter.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.512
- Now, it's turned into Jacob
sounding like a stalker.

00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:32.345
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:33.178
- [Jacob] I know.

00:00:33.178 --> 00:00:34.011
I was so excited.

00:00:34.011 --> 00:00:35.190
I was like, "Sam Smith follows me".

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.210
- No way.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.280
I'm so sorry, I'll
follow you on Instagram,

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.101
because Twitter, I don't do.

00:00:40.101 --> 00:00:41.010
- Okay, cool.
- See, it was somebody else.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.200
- I even dressed in the same color as you.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.160
- I'll DM you.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.170
- Do people still ask you
about "Game of Thrones"

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.261
or just annoying people like me?

00:00:48.261 --> 00:00:49.330
(Kelly laughs)
- You're not annoying.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:51.150
Yeah, no, people do still ask.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.541
- Yeah.
- A lot.

00:00:52.541 --> 00:00:53.820
- [Kelly] It was such a huge thing.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.750
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.320
- Yeah, I mean, I get like a
lot of like, genital questions.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.153
(Sam gasps)

00:00:59.153 --> 00:01:00.390
- Like, what questions?

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.530
- Because I was a eunuch.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.621
- No, I know, oh, my
God, you said genital.

00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:05.454
- [Jacob] Genital.
(Jacob laughs)

00:01:05.454 --> 00:01:06.287
- [Kelly] That's what you said.

00:01:06.287 --> 00:01:07.120
I thought you said general,

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.400
I get a lot of general questions.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.233
I was like, "Like what?"

00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:13.541
And I didn't hear
genital, so now I get it.

00:01:13.541 --> 00:01:14.374
- [Jacob] Yeah.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.480
- I think you're probably fine.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.520
I'm not gonna ask you any
questions about your genitals.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.360
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.350
- Thank you.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.420
- That's amazing.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.520
I was like, "Well, what
are the general questions?"

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.250
I was like, so wait, so
I, I love that though,

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.170
because a lot of people don't like when,

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.270
like, I don't mind when people
bring up "American Idol".

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.640
That's where I'm, I
started in the industry.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.720
I, that's why I don't ever mind,

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.160
because it's like, how I got in the door,

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.750
where people really got to know me.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.583
- [Jacob] Yeah.

00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:38.416
- So, I think it's cool.

00:01:38.416 --> 00:01:40.650
Like that's, your first start
is freaking "Game of Thrones".

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.508
Even if you're a eunuch
with genital problems.

00:01:42.508 --> 00:01:43.389
(audience laughs)

00:01:43.389 --> 00:01:44.970
(Jacob laughs)

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.390
Is it, is it true though,
you once did a scene

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.700
where you had to like speak in Valyrian?

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.410
Is that, did you really have to do that?

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.243
- [Jacob] Oh, yeah.

00:01:53.243 --> 00:01:54.703
Well, I did many, many
scenes in Valyrian, but...

00:01:54.703 --> 00:01:56.880
- But I mean like impromptu.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.411
- I know which one you mean, yeah.

00:01:58.411 --> 00:02:00.000
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.790
So, I was, I've never had to improvise

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.890
in a made up language, not how like...

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:05.723
- Well, nobody has.

00:02:05.723 --> 00:02:06.750
- Who among us?
- Yeah.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.700
- But, so there was one night,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.320
it was like a very stressful scene,

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.360
everyone's getting ready for a battle.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.091
And it's like pitch black, snow

00:02:15.091 --> 00:02:17.069
and the director just
shouts over, he was like,

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:20.160
"Jacob, just improvise something.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.230
Just say something that makes you angry,

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.949
but say it in Valyrian".

00:02:23.949 --> 00:02:26.137
And I like, panicked and
I just started going,

00:02:26.137 --> 00:02:29.157
"Mike Pence, Mike Pence, Mike Pence".

00:02:29.157 --> 00:02:31.320
And I shouted, "Mike Pence".

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.153
- Oh, my...

00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:33.900
- [Jacob] Just over and
over and over again.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.310
- And it wasn't even like political,

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.360
you're just yelling it?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.701
Like, you're just like, "Well..."

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:38.790
(audience laughs)

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.920
- Maybe a little bit political, but, yeah.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.381
- I mean, what a random thing to say.

00:02:43.381 --> 00:02:44.214
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:44.214 --> 00:02:45.047
- I didn't know what to do.

00:02:45.047 --> 00:02:48.360
- What did the other, did
the other cast members laugh?

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.469
- They didn't hear it,
but the director did.

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:51.302
- Oh.
(audience laughs)

00:02:51.302 --> 00:02:53.550
- So, when I came back and
I was like, "Was that okay?"

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.821
And he was like, "Not
really, no, I can't".

00:02:55.821 --> 00:02:56.654
(audience laughs)
- [Kelly] Not really.

00:02:56.654 --> 00:02:58.547
- I can't use that, I was like, "Yeah".

00:02:58.547 --> 00:03:00.570
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.880
- So, wait, you're also a musician

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:03.930
and you have several albums.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.630
So, like I love that about
you, what got you into music?

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.340
- I think I just, like, I've always,

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.461
I grew up in a very musical household.

00:03:10.461 --> 00:03:11.940
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.952
- Like lots of loud music.

00:03:13.952 --> 00:03:15.540
- [Kelly] Love.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.773
What kind of genres?

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.700
- My dad was really into
like, Dob and Roots,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.840
it was like reggae.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:22.794
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:22.794 --> 00:03:24.900
- And like, he'd play it at
like, like insane levels.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.370
Like you just feel bass...

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.600
- Like, 11.
- Rumbling through you.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.433
- Yes.

00:03:28.433 --> 00:03:30.990
- My mom listened to a
lot of house, again bass.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.490
Just all bass.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.020
But I don't make very bassy music,

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.990
I make like very sad
music about my feelings.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.733
By the way you, you were,

00:03:38.733 --> 00:03:42.000
that was such a beautiful
performance that you just did.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:42.878
- Oh, thanks.

00:03:42.878 --> 00:03:43.711
(audience applauds)
- [Jacob] Loved it.

00:03:43.711 --> 00:03:44.940
- I've always wanted to sing with Sam,

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.080
you're so good, you're so good, yeah.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:47.913
(audience applauds)

00:03:47.913 --> 00:03:50.490
Well, congrats, like, I
love "Game of Thrones",

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.530
but I'm so excited about
"Interview with the Vampire".

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.526
Congrats on this, this is awesome.

00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:55.359
(audience applauds)

00:03:55.359 --> 00:03:56.520
So, is it, does it stick closely

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.837
